Write a Python 3 script that acts as a Termux-friendly archive packer and
compression benchmarker built on the py7zr library.
It should be runnable as an executable with the shebang
`#!/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/env python`, and use `from __future__
import annotations` for type hints. **Dependencies and imports:** - Standard
library only, plus `py7zr` (required) and `loguru` (optional).
Use `argparse`, `logging`, `mmap`, `multiprocessing`, `shutil`, `sys`,
`tarfile`, `tempfile`, `concurrent.futures.ProcessPoolExecutor`, `pathlib.Path`,
and `typing` (`Any`, `Dict`, `List`, `Optional`, `Tuple`). - Attempt to import
`loguru`'s logger as `_log`; if the import fails, set `_log` to `None` and fall
back to the standard `logging` module. **Module constants:** -
`_BASIC_SKIP_SUFFIXES`: set of file suffixes to skip in basic mode, namely
`.7z`, `.xz`, `.br`, `.zst`, `.gz`, `.zip`, `.whl`, `.log`. -
`_NAMED_SKIP_SUFFIXES`: set of suffixes to skip in named mode, namely `.tar`,
`.7z`, `.br`, `.gz`, `.xz`, `.zip`, `.whl`. - `_FULL_SKIP_SUFFIXES`: tuple of
suffixes to skip in full mode, namely `.7z`, `.xz`, `.gz`, `.bz2`, `.br`,
`.zst`, `.zip`, `.rar`. - `_NAMED_METHODS`: tuple `("LZMA2", "LZMA", "PPMd")` of
compression methods to try in named mode. - `_FULL_SETTINGS`: a dict of py7zr
write options: an LZMA2 filter at preset 9, dictionary size 268435456 bytes (256
MiB), solid archive enabled, header compression enabled, and block size 4194304
bytes (4 MiB). **Logging helpers:** - Implement `_log_info`, `_log_warning`, and
`_log_error`.
Each takes a message template and optional positional args.
When `_log` is available, format the message with `str.format(*args)` if args
are given and call the loguru method; otherwise pass the template and args
directly to the corresponding `logging` function. **Expected behavior (inferred
from the module design):** - Provide a command-line interface via `argparse`
that accepts an input path (file or directory) and an output location, and
selects a mode (basic, named, or full) that determines which compression methods
and skip-suffix rules apply. - In full mode, use `_FULL_SETTINGS` when writing
7z archives via py7zr. - In named mode, iterate over `_NAMED_METHODS`, trying
each method when creating archives. - Skip files matching the mode's suffix set,
logging skipped items. - Use `tempfile` for intermediate staging and `shutil`
for file operations; use `tarfile` for tar-based packaging where relevant. - Use
`mmap` for efficient reading of large files where appropriate. - Use
`ProcessPoolExecutor` (with `multiprocessing`) to compress multiple files or
variants in parallel, returning results as `(name, result)`-style tuples typed
with `Tuple`, `Dict`, and `List`. - Report sizes and compression ratios per
variant and a summary, and handle errors per item without aborting the whole
run, logging failures through the helpers. - Guard the entry point with `if
__name__ == "__main__":` and exit with `sys.exit` using a nonzero status on
fatal errors. **Edge cases to handle:** missing or unreadable inputs, empty
directories, skipped suffixes, temp-directory cleanup even on failure, and the
optional absence of `loguru`. **Note:** The source was truncated at the
`_log_error` helper, so the remainder of the script (the main logic and CLI)
must be designed to fit these constants and helpers consistently. ---
